            "review_title": "Review at Phu Quoc Seafood Restaurant",
            "review_text": "GLOBETROTTER\nCopenhagen, Denmark214 contributions\n0\nReally nice food, but at least 60% pricecut is needed... Does a manager ever read this?\nJul 2018 • Couples\nDoes not seem to be overwhelmed by customers, we went there the first night of our stay and had a starter and a main course, pricelevel of dishes ranges in general from 80000 to 250.000. We ordered a French chardonnay wine (No local wines available). The cheapest wines around starts at 1.500.000 VND and goes beyond 5 mill. This is a horrendous price level at European Michelin level, which is unacceptable. The food was really good, no complaints at all. The waiter was a disaster: His English was very bad, he had to say “dessert” four times until my wife could figure it out and in general he tried to do it as good as he could, but the list is long: Although he knew we were supposed to have two courses with the bottle of white-wine he served so small amounts of wine in the glasses, what he must have been pouring at least 10 times! Due to this fact and in general we felt “monitored” in a way it made it difficult to enjoy the meal. He asked about our opinion about the food before it hit our bellies and he asked for dessert before taking our plates from the main course. He tried to organize the cutlery several times very precise with no luck. After a while with an incompetent waiter it gets difficult to enjoy the experience and especially at a price like this. This was our first night and considering the competition of a number of restaurants only a few hundred meters away (Which seems to be owned by the same company SEO Group), this is not going to work (message to the hotel manager I guess). A final advice is to teach the waiters English and give them training as being a waiter and finally drop the prices with at least 60% - it must be better to get customers into the restaurant than give bad experiences to very few people, it affects the hotel reputation too!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 6, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
